  "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=sin\u2061x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x)^{\u2032}\\cdot sin\u2061x-x\\cdot (sin\u2061x)^{\u2032}}{{(sin\u2061x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot sin\u2061x-x\\cdot cos\u2061x}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{sin\u2061x-xcos\u2061x}{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
